  author for the current preferred citation.
title: "MOSAIC: Mapping Organizational States Across InterCellular Ecosystems"
abstract: >-
  MOSAIC is a graph-native framework for representing, measuring,
  and interpreting cellular organization in spatial biological data.
  It transforms biological entities into graph representations,
  graph representations into quantitative organizational features,
  and organizational features into interpretable tissue fingerprints.
